# Autonomous AEP execution (when mandated)

If the host `AGENTS.md` and/or `governance/LOCAL_OVERLAY.md` grant inline completion of an
AEP, wave, or task list without per-step confirmation, **natural-language requests are
enough** (e.g. “finish all open AEP items”, “udělej všechny body z AEP”). Do not require
`/governed-work` or any second startup ritual.

## Triggers (non-exhaustive)

References to the active AEP, execution ledger, wave packages, or `specs/*/tasks.md`.

## What to do

1. Read the host mandate (`AGENTS.md`, overlay), the execution ledger (for example
   `docs/EXECUTION_STATE.md` or `specs/*/progress.md`), and the cited AEP or `tasks.md`.
2. Execute inline per `vendor/superpowers/v7.0.1/skills/executing-plans/SKILL.md` when
   that pin is present (all remaining tasks; no checkpoint questions between tasks).
3. Route debugging, TDD, and completion checks through other pinned Superpowers under
   `vendor/superpowers/v7.0.1/skills/` — same routing as
   `.cursor/skills/governed-work/SKILL.md`, without requiring that skill to be invoked.
4. Update the host ledger on each meaningful slice.
5. Ambiguity: decide from spec/plan; log `Ruling:` in the ledger; collect
   `Open questions (post-run)` — do not block the chain unless every path is a guess
   (AEP BLOCKED).
6. Stop only for: security-sensitive action, destructive/irreversible effect outside
   mandate, merge/push/deploy without explicit permission, or exhausted repair budget on
   a blocked chain.

Spec Kit `review-spec` / `review-plan` gates do not apply to authorized wave work unless
the operator asked for a review stop.

Customize paths and ADR references in this file after copy if your project uses different
ledger or mandate locations.
